  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure surface and aloft will provide dry, and increasingly \nmild conditions this week. Valley fog will be possible in the \nmornings, with the cold air/warm water contrast. With temperatures \nanticipated to dip at or below freezing again tonight, freezing fog \nwill be a possibility again. Will allow evening shift to determine \nif another SPS is warranted. \n\nAs mentioned by previous forecaster, main highlight much of this \nweek will be the increasingly dry air, with low afternoon RH as \ndrier air aloft mixes to the surface. Winds however should remain \nquite light, thereby mitigating much in the way of fire weather \nconcerns. \n\nThe next chance for precipitation doesn't arrive until late in the \nweek or early next week. A low will move northeast along the \nAtlantic coast over the weekend. Much of this moisture looks to miss \nus at this point, however, an approaching trough from the west \nduring the period looks more promising in terms of light \nprecipitation.",
